From 8de24e226d745c59972b1898df5cceacf0a7ad47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Jan=20=C4=8Cerm=C3=A1k?= <sairon@sairon.cz>
Date: Tue, 12 May 2026 14:24:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: bcmstb: Fix non-removable check in bcm2712 init

Upstream-Status: Backport [https://source.denx.de/u-boot/u-boot/-/commit/8de24e226d745c59972b1898df5cceacf0a7ad47]

Backported to fix eMMC boot on reComputer R22 (BCM2712/CM5): U-Boot
2026.01 reads host->mmc->host_caps in sdhci_brcmstb_init_2712() before
the MMC uclass populates it, so every BCM2712 SDHCI instance - including
the non-removable eMMC - takes the removable-SD branch and writes
SDIO_CFG_SD_PIN_SEL = SD (0x02). The value persists across SDHCI_RESET_ALL
into Linux, where it racily prevents the SDHCI POWER_ON bit from latching
and wedges the first CMD0 (up to ~20 s eMMC probe delays). Forcing the
presence branch for non-removable / polled hosts leaves SD_PIN_SEL at its
default for the eMMC.

Fixes: 10127cdbab64 ("mmc: bcmstb: Add support for bcm2712 SD controller")
Signed-off-by: Jan Čermák <sairon@sairon.cz>
Reviewed-by: Ivan T. Ivanov <iivanov@suse.de>
(cherry picked from upstream commit 8de24e226d745c59972b1898df5cceacf0a7ad47)
---
 drivers/mmc/bcmstb_sdhci.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/bcmstb_sdhci.c b/drivers/mmc/bcmstb_sdhci.c
index 7bddbebb162..f27b84a6ee4 100644
--- a/drivers/mmc/bcmstb_sdhci.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/bcmstb_sdhci.c
@@ -56,7 +56,7 @@ struct sdhci_brcmstb_dev_priv {
 
 static int sdhci_brcmstb_init_2712(struct udevice *dev)
 {
-	struct sdhci_host *host = dev_get_priv(dev);
+	struct sdhci_bcmstb_plat *plat = dev_get_plat(dev);
 	void *cfg_regs;
 	u32 reg;
 
@@ -65,8 +65,8 @@ static int sdhci_brcmstb_init_2712(struct udevice *dev)
 	if (!cfg_regs)
 		return -ENOENT;
 
-	if ((host->mmc->host_caps & MMC_CAP_NONREMOVABLE) ||
-	    (host->mmc->host_caps & MMC_CAP_NEEDS_POLL)) {
+	if ((plat->cfg.host_caps & MMC_CAP_NONREMOVABLE) ||
+	    (plat->cfg.host_caps & MMC_CAP_NEEDS_POLL)) {
 		/* Force presence */
 		reg = readl(cfg_regs + SDIO_CFG_CTRL);
 		reg &= ~SDIO_CFG_CTRL_SDCD_N_TEST_LEV;
